{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0d1b7611-ca03-4a38-9431-cb7ce11b2164","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97855bad50ea3558","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-8cwhzp0v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Remote pgvector vector_io provider wiring for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the branch-independent provider wiring for the default vector store: Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances are configured to use the remote pgvector vector_io provider — a separate process decoupled from the OGX instance, not an inline provider — reusing the existing remote vector store implementation. The majority of the vector_io integration already exists in the OGX distribution; this epic wires it into the playground's OGXServer instance configuration emitted by the gen-ai BFF. The PostgreSQL instance itself is provisioned by whichever approach the provisioning go/no-go decision selects (operator-based, BFF-managed, or customer-supplied); this epic consumes its connection details and is deliberately not blocked by that decision.\n\n## Scope\n\n- gen-ai BFF configuration of playground OGXServer instances: enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider instead of the inline provider path, on the vector storage configuration surface only\n- Connection-details plumbing abstracted so the source (operator-provisioned, BFF-provisioned, or user-supplied secret) is interchangeable, and a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL connection string can be consumed when it becomes available (RHOAI 3.6) without reworking the provider wiring\n- Per-namespace scoping of vector store namespaces so playgrounds in different namespaces are isolated\n- Keep OGX application storage on its existing default (SQLite) — no consolidation of vector and application storage, and no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration\n- Keep provider selection configurable as the rollback path until inline provider removal (RHAISTRAT-7474) proceeds\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Playground OGX instances created for RAG-enabled playgrounds run the remote pgvector vector_io provider as a separate process from the OGX instance (no inline provider in use)\n- Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows (document ingestion, embedding, retrieval) function end-to-end against a provisioned pgvector instance with no loss of current capability — verified against an instance provisioned by the provisioning approach selected at the go/no-go decision\n- Vector data for playgrounds in different namespaces is isolated (per-namespace scoping)\n- OGX application storage remains on its existing SQLite default; no application-storage migration occurs (vector storage configuration is independent of the application storage backend)\n- The connection-details source is abstracted: swapping it (operator-provisioned, BFF-provisioned, user-supplied, or platform-shared in RHOAI 3.6) requires no change to the provider wiring\n- Provider selection remains configurable, so the inline provider path can be restored as a rollback/fallback if the remote pgvector path fails validation before inline provider removal lands\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\": this epic wires and validates the provider path (end-to-end function additionally requires the selected provisioning branch's instance).\n- **HLR-3 (P0)** — \"The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (not an inline provider)\": delivered by the remote pgvector provider configuration.\n- **HLR-4 (P1)** — \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation)\": delivered in the same configuration surface; kept in this epic because a split would double-touch the same configuration code.\n- **HLR-6 (P2)** — \"Migration path / portability toward production-grade vector databases and the platform-shared PostgreSQL (RHOAI 3.6)\": delivered as the abstracted connection-details source over the existing provider-configurable remote vector store implementation; kept in this epic because it edits the same configuration surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76312,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0adbb6edc27c5f","agent_id":"adc4525af95e71d2b","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"c3e0d893-46e6-498e-a1f4-a650b2d42ac3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:34:32.092Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
