{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7311eef5-ad0c-430f-802b-9e9c0b71fa9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba730b90f36a401e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-8cwhzp0v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n\n## Description\n\nConditional branch, executed only if the provisioning go/no-go decision selects operator-based self-provisioning — i.e., the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time for RHOAI 3.5 and provides the RHOAI-controlled operator layer. PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management for Gen AI Studio lives in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern: each consuming component gets a provisioned database and consumes a connection string rather than self-provisioning. The ogx-k8s-operator is upstream and cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning logic, which is why the operator layer from the modularization is a hard precondition for this branch.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Operator-layer reconciliation of a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance (the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image, `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` — pgvector included, no custom image build) scoped per Gen AI Studio namespace\n- Surfacing of the provisioned database's connection details (secret/connection string) to the playground OGX instance configuration emitted for RAG-enabled playgrounds\n- Full lifecycle management in the operator: provisioning, cleanup on deletion of the owning resource, recovery on pod restart, and credential handling\n- Resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values, adjusted per benchmark findings\n- Disconnected-install support via the PostgreSQL image environment variable already present in the rhods-operator CSV\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance is provisioned automatically per Gen AI Studio namespace by the RHOAI-controlled operator layer when a RAG-enabled playground requires it — no manual user provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure\n- The provisioned instance's connection details are consumed by the playground OGX instance configuration without user intervention\n- Deleting the owning resource cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL instance and its data; pod restarts recover without data loss or manual intervention; credential handling is defined and implemented\n- Resource requests/limits are set from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values as the starting point\n- The PostgreSQL image reference is overridable for disconnected installs (reusing the existing image environment variable in the rhods-operator CSV)\n- The provisioning is scoped per namespace (multi-tenant isolation between namespaces)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\": this branch delivers the out-of-the-box provisioning mechanism.\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\": this branch supplies the instance the wired provider path runs against.\n- **HLR-4 (P1)** — \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation)\": delivered by the per-namespace provisioning scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78133,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0adbb6edc27c5f","agent_id":"adc4525af95e71d2b","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"8cd69221-ddab-4c68-8d2e-14e223bf98e2","timestamp":"2026-10