{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7311eef5-ad0c-430f-802b-9e9c0b71fa9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a712d96bf063c843","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-8cwhzp0v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E003.md","content":"# Bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration support for Gen AI Studio RAG (branch C)\n\n## Description\n\nConditional branch, executed only if the provisioning go/no-go decision selects the bring-your-own outcome — i.e., neither self-provisioning approach is viable for RHOAI 3.5. Customers supply their own PostgreSQL (with pgvector) for RAG capabilities in the Playground by configuring the OGXServer CR spec with their PostgreSQL connection details, consistent with the breaking changes introduced in OGX 1.0. This is the degraded fallback: it does not preserve the fully out-of-the-box experience, and it must solve how customer-supplied connection details surface into playground-created OGXServer instances, since the Playground largely abstracts OGX from users.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Configuration path for customer-supplied PostgreSQL connection details (connection string secret) on the OGXServer CR spec consumed by RAG-enabled playgrounds\n- A surfacing mechanism for the connection details in the Playground experience, since the Playground abstracts OGX from users (the exact surface — administrator-level configuration versus per-playground input — is an implementation decision for the team)\n- Validation of the supplied connection details with actionable error messages when the database is unreachable or lacks pgvector\n- No silent degradation: absence of configuration produces a clear, actionable message rather than a broken RAG experience\n- Customer-facing configuration guidance for the supported PostgreSQL path (kept as scope within this epic; no new documentation topics are authored)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A customer-configured external PostgreSQL (with pgvector) is consumed by RAG-enabled playground workflows via the OGXServer CR spec connection details, with no loss of RAG capability relative to a provisioned instance\n- Invalid, unreachable, or pgvector-missing database configuration is rejected with an actionable error message at configuration time\n- Absence of any PostgreSQL configuration produces a clear actionable message explaining what must be supplied — no silent failure mid-workflow\n- The configuration path is documented sufficiently for customers to complete setup without source-code inspection\n- Customer-supplied instances remain scoped per namespace (multi-tenant isolation between namespaces)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\": this branch only partially satisfies this requirement (customer-supplied database); it is the degraded fallback recorded in the decomposition's health warnings.\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\": this branch supplies the instance the wired provider path runs against, once configured.\n- **HLR-4 (P1)** — \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation)\": delivered by the per-namespace configuration scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78133,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0adbb6edc27c5f","agent_id":"adc4525af95e71d2b","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"812fb2f9-0463-4776-93f0-bd8b52088d78","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:35:03.218Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
