nd RAG workloads (small document sets, flat-scan retrieval) with the measurement setup recorded\n- The remote pgvector default store is measured on the same workloads and is within the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline (order-of-magnitude comparison, not a latency SLA)\n- Recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are documented, starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values and adjusted per the benchmark findings\n- A findings report records the comparison, the sizing recommendation, and the positioning that production-scale vector workloads should use an external vector database\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-5 (P1)** — \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead (order-of-magnitude parity with the inline Milvus baseline; sizing per the model-registry-operator reference)\": fully delivered by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78133,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0adbb6edc27c5f","agent_id":"adc4525af95e71d2b","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"59a3cc89-9fac-48a2-92b8-e205f4a07be0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:35:11.138Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
