{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7163cc2ee15c6a4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Remote pgvector vector_io provider wiring for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Dashboard Crimson Scrum\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Remote pgvector vector_io provider wiring for Gen AI Studio playgrounds\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the branch-independent provider wiring for the default vector store: Gen AI Studio playground OGX instances are configured to use the remote pgvector vector_io provider — a separate process decoupled from the OGX instance, not an inline provider — reusing the existing remote vector store implementation. The majority of the vector_io integration already exists in the OGX distribution; this epic wires it into the playground's OGXServer instance configuration emitted by the gen-ai BFF. The PostgreSQL instance itself is provisioned by whichever approach the provisioning go/no-go decision selects (operator-based, BFF-managed, or customer-supplied); this epic consumes its connection details and is deliberately not blocked by that decision.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- gen-ai BFF configuration of playground OGXServer instances: enable the remote pgvector vector_io provider instead of the inline provider path, on the vector storage configuration surface only\n38\t- Connection-details plumbing abstracted so the source (operator-provisioned, BFF-provisioned, or user-supplied secret) is interchangeable, and a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL connection string can be consumed when it becomes available (RHOAI 3.6) without reworking the provider wiring\n39\t- Per-namespace scoping of vector store namespaces so playgrounds in different namespaces are isolated\n40\t- Keep OGX application storage on its existing default (SQLite) — no consolidation of vector and application storage, and no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration\n41\t- Keep provider selection configurable as the rollback path until inline provider removal (RHAISTRAT-7474) proceeds\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Playground OGX instances created for RAG-enabled playgrounds run the remote pgvector vector_io provider as a separate process from the OGX instance (no inline provider in use)\n46\t- Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows (document ingestion, embedding, retrieval) function end-to-end against a provisioned pgvector instance with no loss of current capability — verified against an instance provisioned by the provisioning approach selected at the go/no-go decision\n47\t- Vector data for playgrounds in different namespaces is isolated (per-namespace scoping)\n48\t- OGX application storage remains on its existing SQLite default; no application-storage migration occurs (vector storage configuration is independent of the application storage backend)\n49\t- The connection-details source is abstracted: swapping it (operator-provisioned, BFF-provisioned, user-supplied, or platform-shared in RHOAI 3.6) requires no change to the provider wiring\n50\t- Provider selection remains configurable, so the inline provider path can be restored as a rollback/fallback if the remote pgvector path fails validation before inline provider removal lands\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\": this epic wires and validates the provider path (end-to-end function additionally requires the selected provisioning branch's instance).\n55\t- **HLR-3 (P0)** — \"The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (not an inline provider)\": delivered by the remote pgvector provider configuration.\n56\t- **HLR-4 (P1)** — \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation)\": delivered in the same configuration surface; kept in this epic because a split would double-touch the same configuration code.\n57\t- **HLR-6 (P2)** — \"Migration path / portability toward production-grade vector databases and the platform-shared PostgreSQL (RHOAI 3.6)\": delivered as the abstracted connection-details source over the existing provider-configurable remote vector store implementation; kept in this epic because it edits the same configuration surface.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ada7191bb267446e","agent_id":"a36f22da151b040d7","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"7a9ad04a-5fda-431e-90a8-928d3066f8ee","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:37:48.635Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7163cc2ee15c6a4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
