{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-892b6270272d1e43","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch\n4\t  A)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Dashboard Crimson Scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n17\t    not land in time for RHOAI 3.5, this operator-based provisioning epic is not executed;\n18\t    fall back to BFF-managed provisioning (preferred alternative) or bring-your-own\n19\t    PostgreSQL per the go/no-go decision record.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 0\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 0\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 1\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConditional branch, executed only if the provisioning go/no-go decision selects operator-based self-provisioning — i.e., the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time for RHOAI 3.5 and provides the RHOAI-controlled operator layer. PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management for Gen AI Studio lives in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern: each consuming component gets a provisioned database and consumes a connection string rather than self-provisioning. The ogx-k8s-operator is upstream and cannot carry this RHOAI-specific provisioning logic, which is why the operator layer from the modularization is a hard precondition for this branch.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Operator-layer reconciliation of a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance (the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image, `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` — pgvector included, no custom image build) scoped per Gen AI Studio namespace\n45\t- Surfacing of the provisioned database's connection details (secret/connection string) to the playground OGX instance configuration emitted for RAG-enabled playgrounds\n46\t- Full lifecycle management in the operator: provisioning, cleanup on deletion of the owning resource, recovery on pod restart, and credential handling\n47\t- Resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values, adjusted per benchmark findings\n48\t- Disconnected-install support via the PostgreSQL image environment variable already present in the rhods-operator CSV\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance is provisioned automatically per Gen AI Studio namespace by the RHOAI-controlled operator layer when a RAG-enabled playground requires it — no manual user provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure\n53\t- The provisioned instance's connection details are consumed by the playground OGX instance configuration without user intervention\n54\t- Deleting the owning resource cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL instance and its data; pod restarts recover without data loss or manual intervention; credential handling is defined and implemented\n55\t- Resource requests/limits are set from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values as the starting point\n56\t- The PostgreSQL image reference is overridable for disconnected installs (reusing the existing image environment variable in the rhods-operator CSV)\n57\t- The provisioning is scoped per namespace (multi-tenant isolation between namespaces)\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\": this branch delivers the out-of-the-box provisioning mechanism.\n62\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — \"Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability\": this branch supplies the instance the wired provider path runs against.\n63\t- **HLR-4 (P1)** — \"The default vector store is scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation)\": delivered by the per-namespace provisioning scope.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ada7191bb267446e","agent_id":"a36f22da151b040d7","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"e6b4eab9-822a-4975-bb7d-20ed6259e5ef","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:37:51.588Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-892b6270272d1e43","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
