{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-921a8c2146b34df7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Provisioning approach go/no-go: operator-based vs BFF-managed vs bring-your-own\n4\t  PostgreSQL for the Gen AI Studio default vector store'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Dashboard Crimson Scrum\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -2\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Provisioning approach go/no-go: operator-based vs BFF-managed vs bring-your-own PostgreSQL for the Gen AI Studio default vector store\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the gating decision for how the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance backing the Gen AI Studio default vector store is provisioned for RHOAI 3.5. Three bounded outcomes exist: (A) operator-based self-provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer, which is only available if the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time; (B) gen-ai BFF-managed provisioning, in which the backend-for-frontend creates the PostgreSQL Deployment, Service, PVC, and Secret when a playground with RAG is configured; or (C) requiring customers to bring their own PostgreSQL via the OGXServer CR spec. The answer determines which downstream provisioning implementation is executed, so the downstream work is modeled as conditional branches selected by this decision. Per Staff Engineer Input, the development team should define this as a go/no-go gate as part of sprint planning.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Assess RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization) delivery status and timing against the RHOAI 3.5 release timeline, with the owning team's commitment\n35\t- Evaluate the BFF-managed alternative against its known lifecycle risks: the BFF is not an operator with a reconciliation loop, so cleanup on playground deletion, handling of pod restarts, and credential rotation need explicit design judgment before it can be selected\n36\t- Confirm the instance image for all approaches: the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`) — no custom image build, no build-pipeline onboarding\n37\t- Confirm the vector store scoping model (per-namespace isolation) in the decision record, given Auto Rag is decoupled from this strategy's scope\n38\t- Produce a decision record naming the selected approach, the go/no-go criteria and evidence that drove it, and the fallback approach if the selected one becomes unworkable during the release cycle\n39\t- Confirm the downstream provisioning scope for the selected approach is executable within the release timeline\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A decision record documents the selected provisioning approach (operator-based, BFF-managed, or bring-your-own PostgreSQL) for the Gen AI Studio default vector store, including the RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery assessment and go/no-go criteria that drove it\n44\t- The decision record evaluates the BFF-managed alternative's lifecycle risks (cleanup on playground deletion, pod-restart recovery, credential rotation) and states why the selected approach was preferred\n45\t- The decision record confirms the scoping model (per-namespace isolation) for the default vector store\n46\t- The decision record names the fallback approach if the selected approach becomes unworkable during the release cycle\n47\t- The downstream provisioning scope for the selected approach is confirmed as executable within the release timeline, so the corresponding conditional branch can be scheduled\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — \"A default vector store is available out-of-the-box on RHOAI without requiring users to manually provision or configure external infrastructure\": this investigation selects the provisioning mechanism that delivers it; the conditional branch epics execute the selected mechanism.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a7fa116272e39e4","agent_id":"abb1e55ed789b4799","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"9e0edf6d-a2dd-4a9e-8a4e-dc537258a3f0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:08.247Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-921a8c2146b34df7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
