{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5157db56482f849","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E004\n3\ttitle: pgvector benchmark and resource sizing validation for the default vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Dashboard Crimson Scrum\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 0\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# pgvector benchmark and resource sizing validation for the default vector store\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic validates that the pgvector-backed default vector store is lightweight enough for the platform's purposes, in the dev-experimentation scope defined by Staff Engineer Input: the sprint-1 benchmark captures the inline Milvus baseline for representative playground RAG workloads and verifies pgvector lands in the same order of magnitude — strict latency SLAs (p50/p95/p99) are explicitly not required. It also produces the recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits, starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values and adjusting based on the benchmark findings. The default instance targets development experimentation; users with production-scale vector workloads are directed to an external vector database.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Benchmark harness/workload representing typical Playground RAG usage: small document sets, flat scan (no vector index) as the default retrieval path\n39\t- Capture of the inline Milvus provider baseline on the same workloads for comparison\n40\t- Measurement of the remote pgvector provider on the same workloads, verified to be within the same order of magnitude as the baseline (not a threshold/SLA target)\n41\t- Recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits for the provisioned instance, derived from the model-registry-operator's reference values and the benchmark findings\n42\t- A recorded findings report supporting the sizing decision and the dev-experimentation positioning\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- The inline Milvus baseline is captured for representative playground RAG workloads (small document sets, flat-scan retrieval) with the measurement setup recorded\n47\t- The remote pgvector default store is measured on the same workloads and is within the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline (order-of-magnitude comparison, not a latency SLA)\n48\t- Recommended PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are documented, starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values and adjusted per the benchmark findings\n49\t- A findings report records the comparison, the sizing recommendation, and the positioning that production-scale vector workloads should use an external vector database\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- **HLR-5 (P1)** — \"The default vector store is lightweight enough to run in resource-constrained environments without imposing significant overhead (order-of-magnitude parity with the inline Milvus baseline; sizing per the model-registry-operator reference)\": fully delivered by this epic.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a7fa116272e39e4","agent_id":"abb1e55ed789b4799","session_id":"9929ed70-9f3a-43fc-bc5e-5275c2fe8952","uuid":"fe5745db-f53a-49cf-8aef-d3252f3fbd77","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:14.285Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5157db56482f849","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
