ailable strategy text declares no Documentation Support requirement, branch C keeps config guidance as in-epic scope, and the summary flags re-checking the unavailable attachment's Prerequisites & Process Gates before execution (see Criterion 7 note).\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\nAll epics use canonical component \"Gen AI Studio\" and one team (Dashboard Crimson Scrum, inferred from the strategy label since the Impacted Teams table is in the missing attachment — inference recorded in the summary). No epic spans multiple components or teams in a way that bundles others' work; no epic is oversized (each is a single logical change on one surface — BFF config wiring, one benchmark, one provisioning mechanism); no re-split triggers are needed since no overage is claimed. The three branch epics are mutually exclusive conditional alternatives gated by one decision — the sanctioned conditional-branch pattern, not scope duplication; E002 (wiring) and the branches (provisioning) touch complementary surfaces with the coupling expressed as an AC gate. No work-product type mixing: branch C's customer-facing configuration guidance is scoped as part of the config deliverable with no new documentation topics authored. One minor: branch A's work lands in the operator layer delivered by RHAISTRAT-7164 (\"AI Core Dashboard\" territory), and the team/component attribution to Gen AI Studio / Dashboard Crimson Scrum is an acknowledged inference — the decomposition itself flags \"verify at planning\" in Health Warnings, which is the right handling of an unverifiable assignment.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (operator-based vs BFF-managed vs bring-your-own) determines which downstream branch epic exists — it passes the changes-downstream-structure test, and the ≤3 bounded outcomes are correctly modeled as conditional branches with `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` and a populated `fallback_approach` on each branch. All `gated_by` targe